<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfred Meyer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1891–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfred Meyer was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazi Party</a> official who was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauleiter">Gauleiter</a> of Westphalia-North and from 1933 Reich governor of Lippe and Schaumburg-Lippe. From 1941 he was also deputy to Alfred Rosenberg in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reich-ministry-for-the-occupied-eastern-territories">Reich Ministry for the Occupied Eastern Territories</a>, and he attended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wannsee-conference">Wannsee Conference</a> in 1942. He took his own life in April 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-meyer.jpg" alt="Alfred Meyer" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-1991-0712-500,_Alfred_Meyer_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
